ed_at":"2021-12-02T01:50:28Z","updated_at":"2021-12-03T15:34:54Z","closed_at":"2021-12-03T15:34:53Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Describe the bug\n\nExtending a list of sqlalchemy objects with themselves runs forever, i.e. list += list doesn't terminate.\n\n### To Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom sqlalchemy import Column, ForeignKey, Integer, String\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import declarative_base, relationship\r\n\r\nBase = declarative_base()\r\n\r\n\r\nclass Company(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = \"company\"\r\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\r\n    employees = relationship(\"User\", uselist=True, back_populates=\"company\")\r\n    name = Column(String)\r\n\r\n\r\nclass User(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = \"user\"\r\n\r\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\r\n    email = Column(String, nullable=False, unique=True)\r\n\r\n    company_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey(\"company.id\"))\r\n    company = relationship(\"Company\", back_populates=\"employees\")\r\n\r\n\r\ncompany = Company(name=\"test company\")\r\n\r\nuser1 = User(email=\"test\")\r\nuser2 = User(email=\"test2\")\r\nuser3 = User(email=\"test3\")\r\n\r\ncompany.employees = [user1, user2, user3]\r\n\r\ntestlist = company.employees\r\ntestlist += company.employees\r\nprint(\"Finished\")\n```\n\n\n### Error\n\nNo output.\n\n### Versions\n\n- OS: Linux Mint 20.2\r\n- Python: Python 3.8.10\r\n- SQLAlchemy: 1.4.27\r\n- Database: n/a (also tested with sqlite)\r\n- DBAPI (eg: psycopg, cx_oracle, mysqlclient): n/a\r\n\n\n### Additional context\n\nChanging line 32 (testlist = company.employees) to testlist = company.employees.copy() fixes the problem. Otherwise the program runs forever.","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://